Hi Michael,

On Fri, 6 Oct 2023 09:42:40 +1300 Michael Cree <mcree@orcon.net.nz>=20
wrote:
> I have tried the suggested script (with a small modification to count=20
> number of failures) running for a few hours on one of the packages=20
> that had failed on the buildd and never saw cmake fail.
>
> But then building a few packages locally with sbuild, apbs failed=20
> first time to build with the cmake failure.  Second try at=20
> building apbs with sbuild succeeded.
>
> So it appears that there is something different about running in=20
> sbuild (or possibly under dpkg-buildpackage) that is triggering=20
> this failure on occassion.

Thank you for your effort!

Assuming this is somehow related to the actual package build,=20
debhelper injects a number of additional CLI arguments, mostly=20
setting global variables that affect CMake's default behavior:

  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=3D/usr
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=3DNone
  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_SYSCONFDIR=3D/etc
  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LOCALSTATEDIR=3D/var
  -DCMAKE_EXPORT_NO_PACKAGE_REGISTRY=3DON
  -DCMAKE_FIND_USE_PACKAGE_REGISTRY=3DOFF
  -DCMAKE_FIND_PACKAGE_NO_PACKAGE_REGISTRY=3DON
  -DFETCHCONTENT_FULLY_DISCONNECTED=3DON
  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_RUNSTATEDIR=3D/run
  -DCMAKE_SKIP_INSTALL_ALL_DEPENDENCY=3DON
  -DCMAKE_VERBOSE_MAKEFILE=3DON
  -DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=3Dlib/alpha-linux-gnu
  -G"Unix Makefiles"

None of that should be affecting find_library(), but...


Cheers
Timo


